-- pending: #682 (a generator that yields sub-slices of borrowed text, holding its position across `yield`)
-- now: 39:3: the call's result mentions the lifetime of the lent array other than as the view it hands back, so the array cannot be handed back after it
-- Hard problem 14: a tokenizer. `words` is given a borrowed byte string and yields each word as a
-- view of the string itself, at the borrow's lifetime, not as a copy. Between `yield`s it holds
-- the rest of the string, a sub-slice of the one it was given. The consumer keeps the longest
-- word seen so far, a view yielded by an earlier step, across later steps.
--
-- Issue: #682 (views derived from a borrow, held across a suspension and handed out of it).
--
-- Rust: `s.split(' ')`, an iterator whose items are `&'a str` and which holds the remaining
-- `&'a str`; the consumer may keep any item for as long as `'a`.
--
-- Today: refused at `words(&text)`: the generator's elements mention the lifetime of the lend made
-- for the call, so the array cannot be handed back after it. Both backends stop at the same
-- message.
--
-- Once it lands: i32[5]: the longest word of "a quick fox" is "quick"; `live 0`.

include yield
include slice

-- The words of `s`, separated by single spaces, each a view of `s`.
fn words<'a>(s: array_imm 'a u8) -> 1 with Yield[array_imm 'a u8] =
  let mut rest = s;
  let mut more = true;
  while more {
    match find(rest, b' ', !{ (x, y) -> x == y }) {
      inl i -> match split_at(rest, i) {
          inl (w, tail) -> yield(w); match split_first(tail) { inl (sp, t) -> rest = t | inr u -> more = false }
        | inr r -> more = false }
    | inr u -> yield(rest); more = false
    }
  };
  ()

main -> i32 =
  let text = "a quick fox";
  let mut best = 0;
  for w in words(&text) { if len(w) > best { best = len(w) } else { () } };
  best
